From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cheaper PBR shaders

Same images for less GPU work. PBR vertex shaders transform points by
the model rows and the view, and normals by the model's cofactors; the
fragment shader takes the inverse view from the rigid view matrix.
They inverted two 4x4 matrices per vertex and passed a constant 3x3
matrix as a varying. Pen texture coordinates are read only in a
"#define PEN" twin of a program, compiled the first time a Pen paints
one of its materials. Impostors test their coverage at the top of the
fragment shader, everywhere on the quad, and discard before depth,
normals and light.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0044-vertex-transforms: forest view 92.7 -> 89.1 ms, opaque 66.7 ->
  62.6 ms
- 0058-pen-shader-variant: forest view 67.2 -> 65.2 ms, overview 49.2 ->
  47.8 ms
- 0070-impostor-coverage-first: overview -0.45 ms
---
